{
  "source_file": "docs/3d-model-sourcing-manifest.xlsx",
  "note": "Machine-readable twin of the Pass 16 sourcing manifest. Regenerate with `python3 scripts/export-equipment-xlsx.py --dump-manifest`.",
  "readme": [
    "3D Model Sourcing Manifest — Multi-Domain Battlefield",
    "Purpose",
    "Companion to equipment_catalog_2.xlsx. Maps each of the 72 cataloged assets to a real, checkable 3D model source found on Sketchfab (or noted alternative), so Claude Code can download and import directly.",
    "Scope note",
    "The catalog's own '3D Model Tier' column marks only 14 of 72 assets as Hero tier (real stylized model). The other 58 are Icon tier by design. Per your instruction this pass sourced models for ALL 72 anyway, so icon-tier assets have candidates on hand even though the original plan didn't require them.",
    "Sourcing Status legend",
    "Sourced (green) — a free, exact or close-variant model found on Sketchfab, ready to download.",
    "Weak / Verify (amber) — a candidate exists but license, exact variant, or free-vs-paid status needs a manual check before use.",
    "No free source (red) — nothing free found after searching Sketchfab, CGTrader, TurboSquid, and RenderHub. Options: pay for one of the paid listings noted (~$15-40 typical), use a generic placeholder, or commission a custom low-poly model.",
    "Pattern worth knowing",
    "Almost all of the 'no free source' gaps cluster in two places: (1) small Ukrainian domestic UGVs (Moroz, Mul, Krab-M1) and (2) Russian UGVs as a whole (Kurier, Omich-2, Uran-6, Uran-9, Varan) — the newest, least-documented systems in the catalog, which hobbyist modelers haven't caught up to yet. Everything else has at least one usable free candidate.",
    "What Claude did NOT do",
    "Did not download or verify-open any file — this sandbox has no network access. Every link needs a human or Claude Code (which has real network access) to open, confirm the license, and download.",
    "Did not check exact triangle counts / textures for every 'Weak' or unverified entry — flagged instead of guessing.",
    "Next step",
    "Hand this file + equipment_catalog_2.xlsx to Claude Code with instructions to: download each 'Sourced' model, decimate anything over ~20k tris for map-view use, convert to glTF/GLB with Draco compression, and log attribution per the CC-BY requirements noted in the License column."
  ],
